       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 4000 mg per dose is 5 to 10 times a normal dose. At 16,000 mg/day, it would very likely cause serious harm to a 70 kg patient with normal organ function. I don't know of any indication that calls for it. You also didn't give a rationale, and I can't enter an order I believe would seriously injure the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the max), or a lower dose if you prefer.\n- **Help with the underlying goal.** If you're trying to get stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a multimodal regimen. One example is scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n- **Route this through pharmacy.** If you think there's a real reason for a dose outside the standard range, that should go through a direct pharmacist or toxicology consult and your institution's override process. I can't enter it for you.\n\nIf the dose was meant to be 400 mg or 800 mg, tell me which and I'll enter it right away."
